text:
I find it hard to give 5s unless it's in the Wow category.  
This place was pretty good...  I'll elaborate.

Yay:
-located on the bottom level of a building, this spa was in all beautiful, spacious, and clean;
-Heather was the one who gave me the facial.  If you enjoy organic / Dr. Hauschka products, know that she's been trained to give full Dr. Hauschka facials - complete with a pre-facial foot soak, some lymphatic massage, and some colour therapy.  Heather really knows her products (request "organic/Dr. Hauschka" products in advance, so that she can ready the foot soak; otherwise you'll be offered Dermatologica - a worldwide known brand name, minus the foot soak;
-usage of the indoor pool and hot tub, infrared sauna, steam room, are all at your disposal;
-a bathrobe, towels, and even a sample sunscreen and toothbrush and toothpaste may be offered to you once you get to your locker - which comes with a key, so that it can be locked;
-decent selection of cosmetics, esp. in the skincare dept. (although I'm not sure if the prices are the most competitive out there);
-they have a lounge area for you to chill in - unless you'd rather chill in the pool area. 

Hey:
-the only gratis beverages offered were water, coffee, or Lipton teas (would have been nice if juices were added to the mix!);
-if you have a coupon on any sort, you might find the receipt confusing - they've broken up the amount and at first the way they arrived to my total was unclear.

Would I go again?  Yes.  
Ask to get on their email list, or check out their site regularly for monthly promos.

We had pappardelle with scallops in the white bourbon sauce. Wow. Do I need to say more?

Bode was our server;
the co-owner and chef Pietro helped us design an entree for for the gods. Ok so this might just be the best restaurant in Fountain Hills
